{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd...fd3e66c71ccfd4f7383904baa19e5bd700993a05","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd...fd3e66c71ccfd4f7383904baa19e5bd700993a05","permalink_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/OmniNode-ai:2f123b4...OmniNode-ai:fd3e66c","diff_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd...fd3e66c71ccfd4f7383904baa19e5bd700993a05.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd...fd3e66c71ccfd4f7383904baa19e5bd700993a05.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd","node_id":"C_kwDOR6jjtdoAKDJmMTIzYjRjMDFlYWJkMmM1MWY3ZDcwMzQ5MWU5Y2RmMzZmODliY2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai","date":"2026-08-31T06:43:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-31T06:43:09Z"},"message":"feat(OMN-17019): obligation-kind work events + open-obligations projection (C9) (#2227)\n\n* feat(OMN-17019): obligation-kind work events + open-obligations projection\n\nC9 of the OMN-16176 ledger ladder. Replaces \"a markdown file is the goal and\nqueue authority\" with typed obligation events and a materialized projection.\n\nFive obligation kinds (created / transferred / satisfied / superseded /\nabandoned) registered in the emit registry under the EXISTING\nonex.evt.omniclaude.* producer namespace -- no bespoke topic family -- all\npartitioned on obligation_id and all duty_critical, because obligation writes\nfail closed.\n\nnode_projection_open_obligations folds them into\nomninode_internal.open_obligations, one row per obligation. Each kind writes\nonly the columns its kind owns; state and owed_by are GENERATED columns over\nthose facts. That is what makes a consumer restarting from an earlier\npartition offset unable to reopen a closed obligation -- the case a writable\nstate column would silently get wrong.\n\nobligations_view.py renders the B1/B2/A6/A14 surfaces as pure functions over\nthe projection, with render/parse exact inverses so \"delete it and regenerate\nit\" is mechanically testable.\n\nNo expiry, no TTL, no DELETE anywhere: an obligation leaves the open set only\nvia a recorded terminal event naming its own evidence.\n\n* test(OMN-17019): advance the two registry-growth ratchets deliberately\n\nThe full-suite escalation surfaced two ratchets that exist precisely to force\na deliberate decision when the emit registry grows, and the five new\nwork-obligation kinds tripped both. Both are advanced here with the decision\nrecorded, not auto-followed.\n\n1. _DUTY_CRITICAL_ALLOWLIST gains the five obligation kinds. duty_critical is\n   the load-bearing choice of this ticket -- an obligation READ may degrade to\n   the last-good projection and say so, but an obligation WRITE fails closed;\n   the telemetry tier permits exactly the silent drop C9 exists to end. The\n   ratchet's max_payload obligation is specific to the two CAPTURE topics,\n   which carry arbitrary artifact/tool output; every field of an obligation\n   event is a short scalar, bounded by its own schema.\n\n2. test_enrichment_parity's four counts move 62->67 event types and 65->70\n   published records / enriched records, with the null-key remainder frozen at\n   2 because all five obligation kinds declare partition_key_field:\n   obligation_id. Raising these WIDENS the byte-identical parity proof to\n   cover the new kinds rather than excusing them from it -- the mismatched\n   assertion still runs over all 67.\n\n* fix(OMN-17019): bind open obligations publish topic in handler\n\n* fix(OMN-17019): mark open-obligations applied event terminal\n\n* chore(OMN-17019): bump package version for release identity","tree":{"sha":"f2684e63e3cab4e4430af47dc315c5a134fefa99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/trees/f2684e63e3cab4e4430af47dc315c5a134fefa99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/commits/2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlSJ9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAss4QAA4VMn+iinUG5iBR3+LuikxA\nPVr+nQPyUgxryCg2wJMa5YY1mhaP+w5ASw1GOQwb7Jt9scr0oa7KK0CSIaXPOWdC\nVu+eVY6je7xwJorhMWAZMgOayEAO1TXayZvyTHodDwLMIFDGQIfwv+N7Iu2Mxtqi\nUuuCDN99vIKiHzNXCqRFJo5Y6s7K3dCx1PlBuYfbT5j2+O24cazCGx+Xk472/yxT\n+D7dNLPT5+gNhX1FexqI96yQU0QmExGV3rp2WwJt5FmLntrP3ZJD70VKXCjK/TMk\nQgL33tuUHCYNMthiKi7megQ5g6DG6Op1R/c6R7szhODuuOs/f5FpEE+uaG6KePeh\nDdCegwh9iclRDA4ZWmxQHj7mVBQjO6O2UGPyz/oUI5wPk0DIDZXspzajZabhr+FC\nckghbEGzRvSMBO6OFXdeztWWsHCihJJ3HZIgB9hppS5/2kiIptfdif901/F2NCcP\nS1Lk6TTHDyc3Tvf/Bm1PU5vz+Tv40zi7Ak5dGgpn0acQkCiKpj3hlHjjYy3fDm6V\nLdBo76S0o1v/a/XJx3zNW6A0FjdubXbfOPjzm1H+xFRYfNzunY7xwZA9l7jTHjV1\nsXGlbsjmEbbwMdsBuWNskFzbnSzIVZCN1SIEXWgArHfGVXh35zQiEOvyFWN2EKKD\nqck/LReMKaBKmAlQzMm7\n=JRh0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f2684e63e3cab4e4430af47dc315c5a134fefa99\nparent 4dcd92ee5f6a7d21339e0f3d599bc1fe94d357f1\nauthor Jonah Gray <jonah@omninode.ai> 1788158589 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788158589 +0000\n\nfeat(OMN-17019): obligation-kind work events + open-obligations projection (C9) (#2227)\n\n* feat(OMN-17019): obligation-kind work events + open-obligations projection\n\nC9 of the OMN-16176 ledger ladder. Replaces \"a markdown file is the goal and\nqueue authority\" with typed obligation events and a materialized projection.\n\nFive obligation kinds (created / transferred / satisfied / superseded /\nabandoned) registered in the emit registry under the EXISTING\nonex.evt.omniclaude.* producer namespace -- no bespoke topic family -- all\npartitioned on obligation_id and all duty_critical, because obligation writes\nfail closed.\n\nnode_projection_open_obligations folds them into\nomninode_internal.open_obligations, one row per obligation. Each kind writes\nonly the columns its kind owns; state and owed_by are GENERATED columns over\nthose facts. That is what makes a consumer restarting from an earlier\npartition offset unable to reopen a closed obligation -- the case a writable\nstate column would silently get wrong.\n\nobligations_view.py renders the B1/B2/A6/A14 surfaces as pure functions over\nthe projection, with render/parse exact inverses so \"delete it and regenerate\nit\" is mechanically testable.\n\nNo expiry, no TTL, no DELETE anywhere: an obligation leaves the open set only\nvia a recorded terminal event naming its own evidence.\n\n* test(OMN-17019): advance the two registry-growth ratchets deliberately\n\nThe full-suite escalation surfaced two ratchets that exist precisely to force\na deliberate decision when the emit registry grows, and the five new\nwork-obligation kinds tripped both. Both are advanced here with the decision\nrecorded, not auto-followed.\n\n1. _DUTY_CRITICAL_ALLOWLIST gains the five obligation kinds. duty_critical is\n   the load-bearing choice of this ticket -- an obligation READ may degrade to\n   the last-good projection and say so, but an obligation WRITE fails closed;\n   the telemetry tier permits exactly the silent drop C9 exists to end. The\n   ratchet's max_payload obligation is specific to the two CAPTURE topics,\n   which carry arbitrary artifact/tool output; every field of an obligation\n   event is a short scalar, bounded by its own schema.\n\n2. test_enrichment_parity's four counts move 62->67 event types and 65->70\n   published records / enriched records, with the null-key remainder frozen at\n   2 because all five obligation kinds declare partition_key_field:\n   obligation_id. Raising these WIDENS the byte-identical parity proof to\n   cover the new kinds rather than excusing them from it -- the mismatched\n   assertion still runs over all 67.\n\n* fix(OMN-17019): bind open obligations publish topic in handler\n\n* fix(OMN-17019): mark open-obligations applied event terminal\n\n* chore(OMN-17019): bump package version for release identity","verified_at":"2026-08-31T06:43:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4dcd92ee5f6a7d21339e0f3d599bc1fe94d357f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/4dcd92ee5f6a7d21339e0f3d599bc1fe94d357f1","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/4dcd92ee5f6a7d21339e0f3d599bc1fe94d357f1"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd","node_id":"C_kwDOR6jjtdoAKDJmMTIzYjRjMDFlYWJkMmM1MWY3ZDcwMzQ5MWU5Y2RmMzZmODliY2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai","date":"2026-08-31T06:43:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-31T06:43:09Z"},"message":"feat(OMN-17019): obligation-kind work events + open-obligations projection (C9) (#2227)\n\n* feat(OMN-17019): obligation-kind work events + open-obligations projection\n\nC9 of the OMN-16176 ledger ladder. Replaces \"a markdown file is the goal and\nqueue authority\" with typed obligation events and a materialized projection.\n\nFive obligation kinds (created / transferred / satisfied / superseded /\nabandoned) registered in the emit registry under the EXISTING\nonex.evt.omniclaude.* producer namespace -- no bespoke topic family -- all\npartitioned on obligation_id and all duty_critical, because obligation writes\nfail closed.\n\nnode_projection_open_obligations folds them into\nomninode_internal.open_obligations, one row per obligation. Each kind writes\nonly the columns its kind owns; state and owed_by are GENERATED columns over\nthose facts. That is what makes a consumer restarting from an earlier\npartition offset unable to reopen a closed obligation -- the case a writable\nstate column would silently get wrong.\n\nobligations_view.py renders the B1/B2/A6/A14 surfaces as pure functions over\nthe projection, with render/parse exact inverses so \"delete it and regenerate\nit\" is mechanically testable.\n\nNo expiry, no TTL, no DELETE anywhere: an obligation leaves the open set only\nvia a recorded terminal event naming its own evidence.\n\n* test(OMN-17019): advance the two registry-growth ratchets deliberately\n\nThe full-suite escalation surfaced two ratchets that exist precisely to force\na deliberate decision when the emit registry grows, and the five new\nwork-obligation kinds tripped both. Both are advanced here with the decision\nrecorded, not auto-followed.\n\n1. _DUTY_CRITICAL_ALLOWLIST gains the five obligation kinds. duty_critical is\n   the load-bearing choice of this ticket -- an obligation READ may degrade to\n   the last-good projection and say so, but an obligation WRITE fails closed;\n   the telemetry tier permits exactly the silent drop C9 exists to end. The\n   ratchet's max_payload obligation is specific to the two CAPTURE topics,\n   which carry arbitrary artifact/tool output; every field of an obligation\n   event is a short scalar, bounded by its own schema.\n\n2. test_enrichment_parity's four counts move 62->67 event types and 65->70\n   published records / enriched records, with the null-key remainder frozen at\n   2 because all five obligation kinds declare partition_key_field:\n   obligation_id. Raising these WIDENS the byte-identical parity proof to\n   cover the new kinds rather than excusing them from it -- the mismatched\n   assertion still runs over all 67.\n\n* fix(OMN-17019): bind open obligations publish topic in handler\n\n* fix(OMN-17019): mark open-obligations applied event terminal\n\n* chore(OMN-17019): bump package version for release identity","tree":{"sha":"f2684e63e3cab4e4430af47dc315c5a134fefa99","url":"https://api.github.